From: FlaxAdvisors
Subject: sol: fix obmc-console service path match string in registerSOLServiceChangeCallback

The match string "_6fbmc_2dconsole" is an incorrect D-Bus path encoding.
D-Bus path encoding keeps alphanumeric characters (including 'o' = 0x6f)
as-is. On TiogaPass, the active console service is obmc-console@ttyS3,
whose D-Bus path component is "obmc_2dconsole_40ttyS3". The old string
contains no substring match for this path.

Without this fix, matchPtrSOL stays null on every call because
getDbusObject throws "Failed to find object which matches".
registerSOLServiceChangeCallback() is called on every console byte
received (because matchPtrSOL == nullptr), flooding the journal with:
  "Failed to find object which matches"
  "Failed to get service path in registerSOLServiceChangeCallback"

--- a/sol/sol_manager.cpp
+++ b/sol/sol_manager.cpp
@@ -238,7 +238,7 @@ void registerSOLServiceChangeCallback()
     try
     {
         auto servicePath = ipmi::getDbusObject(
             bus, "xyz.openbmc_project.Control.Service.Attributes",
-            "/xyz/openbmc_project/control/service", "_6fbmc_2dconsole");
+            "/xyz/openbmc_project/control/service", "obmc_2dconsole_40ttyS3");

         if (!std::empty(servicePath.first))
         {
